{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RpfxG8GPxgVN8TmCJqzzwU","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n \"number\": 37,\n \"title\": \"restrictOwnAudio is not respected by electron when sharing screen with system audio\",\n \"body\": \"### Preflight Checklist\\n\\n- [x] I have read the [Contributing Guidelines](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) for this project.\\n- [x] I agree to follow the [Code of Conduct](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) that this project adheres to.\\n- [x] I have searched the [issue tracker](https://www.github.com/electron/electron/issues) for a bug report that matches the one I want to file, without success.\\n\\n### Electron Version\\n\\n43.2.0\\n\\n### What operating system(s) are you using?\\n\\nWindows\\n\\n### Operating System Version\\n\\nWindows 11\\n\\n### What arch are you using?\\n\\nx64\\n\\n### Last Known Working Electron version\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Does the issue also appear in Chromium / Google Chrome?\\n\\nNo\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen sharing a screen with system audio on Windows 11 passing the restrictOwnAudio should result in the screen share not capturing audio from the electron window that started the screen share.\\n\\n### Actual Behavior\\n\\nWhen sharing a screen with system audio on Windows 11 passing the restrictOwnAudio does not remove audio coming from the electron window in the stream, creating an echo.\\n\\n### Testcase Gist URL\\n\\nhttps://gist.github.com/Dadadah/9908f615023841b622b45498038a33af\\n\\n### Additional Information\\n\\nClicking share in the fiddle linked in the gist will result in your first screen being shared on the document, which will then echo for a while upon playing a sound.\\n\\nWhen opening index.html and clicking share in chromium, sharing screen and audio, there is only a single echo (the audio is copied once, but not again)\",\n \"labels\": [\n  \"43-x-y\",\n  \"bug :beetle:\",\n  \"has-repro-gist\",\n  \"platform/windows\"\n ],\n \"state\": \"open\",\n \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n \"as_of\": \"2026-07-23T02:09:29Z\",\n \"replay\": true\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"410143f4-c26a-40fd-b46b-883b54287159","uuid":"2893ea8a-9007-4caa-86c4-e661d3439808","timestamp":"2026-10-23T09:47:09.777Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n \"number\": 37,\n \"title\": \"restrictOwnAudio is not respected by electron when sharing screen with system audio\",\n \"body\": \"### Preflight Checklist\\n\\n- [x] I have read the [Contributing Guidelines](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) for this project.\\n- [x] I agree to follow the [Code of Conduct](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) that this project adheres to.\\n- [x] I have searched the [issue tracker](https://www.github.com/electron/electron/issues) for a bug report that matches the one I want to file, without success.\\n\\n### Electron Version\\n\\n43.2.0\\n\\n### What operating system(s) are you using?\\n\\nWindows\\n\\n### Operating System Version\\n\\nWindows 11\\n\\n### What arch are you using?\\n\\nx64\\n\\n### Last Known Working Electron version\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Does the issue also appear in Chromium / Google Chrome?\\n\\nNo\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen sharing a screen with system audio on Windows 11 passing the restrictOwnAudio should result in the screen share not capturing audio from the electron window that started the screen share.\\n\\n### Actual Behavior\\n\\nWhen sharing a screen with system audio on Windows 11 passing the restrictOwnAudio does not remove audio coming from the electron window in the stream, creating an echo.\\n\\n### Testcase Gist URL\\n\\nhttps://gist.github.com/Dadadah/9908f615023841b622b45498038a33af\\n\\n### Additional Information\\n\\nClicking share in the fiddle linked in the gist will result in your first screen being shared on the document, which wil